            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0275" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.0012Anti-War/211: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-16T10:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 16,
                                1928—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 16—5:44
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>82. My telegram No. 81, August 4, 1 p.m.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d122-f1"/> Foreign
                    Office informs me that Grandi finds it will be impossible for him to go to Paris
                    August 27th.</p>
                <p>Italian Ambassador at Paris will sign.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
